WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.960
Kathleen and Mabel were still at their tea party.

2
00:00:06.961 --> 00:00:09.710
Suddenly they both felt the same way.

3
00:00:09.711 --> 00:00:13.293
They must go to the Temple of Flora!

4
00:00:13.294 --> 00:00:17.137
They didn't know why, but they knew they must go.

5
00:00:17.138 --> 00:00:23.532
When Gerald and Jimmy yelled for help, Kathleen and Mabel were ready to help.

6
00:00:23.533 --> 00:00:28.292
The girls opened the door, and the boys were free.

7
00:00:28.293 --> 00:00:31.667
Kathleen hugged her brothers.

8
00:00:31.668 --> 00:00:37.305
They spoke about their adventures in London and in the secret passage.

9
00:00:37.306 --> 00:00:42.271
"Did you leave that Ugly-Wugly in London?" asked Mabel.

10
00:00:42.272 --> 00:00:45.065
"Yes," said Gerald.

11
00:00:45.066 --> 00:00:50.065
"Now we'll seal the ring in an envelope so no one else gets in trouble."

12
00:00:50.066 --> 00:00:55.425
"But I didn't have a chance to use it," protested Kathleen.

13
00:00:55.426 --> 00:00:58.818
"You've seen what it does," said Gerald.

14
00:00:58.819 --> 00:01:01.746
"Why would you want to use it?"

15
00:01:01.747 --> 00:01:06.516
"I'd make it do nice things," said Kathleen.

16
00:01:06.517 --> 00:01:10.933
"Let's just put it back in the treasure room," said Mabel.

17
00:01:10.934 --> 00:01:15.652
"It was a bad idea to take it."

18
00:01:15.653 --> 00:01:19.047
They walked over to the castle.

19
00:01:19.048 --> 00:01:22.764
In the treasure room, Mabel pushed the secret button.

20
00:01:22.765 --> 00:01:26.431
The panels slid up.

21
00:01:26.432 --> 00:01:29.972
All the jewels sparkled on the shelves.

22
00:01:29.973 --> 00:01:33.902
Mabel took the ring from Gerald.

23
00:01:33.903 --> 00:01:38.777
"I don't even know what to call that ring," said Kathleen.

24
00:01:38.778 --> 00:01:43.148
"The wishing ring? The invisibility ring?"

25
00:01:43.149 --> 00:01:48.257
"Oh!" Mabel put the ring on. "I understand now.

26
00:01:48.258 --> 00:01:50.547
The ring is whatever you say it is.

27
00:01:50.548 --> 00:01:53.952
It made us invisible because I said that's what it does.

28
00:01:53.953 --> 00:02:02.185
Then it became a wishing ring during our play."

29
00:02:02.186 --> 00:02:06.085
"It's still a wishing ring," said Jimmy.

30
00:02:06.086 --> 00:02:10.147
"No," said Mabel. "We've already had that.

31
00:02:10.148 --> 00:02:15.608
I say it's a ring that makes the wearer four meters high."

32
00:02:15.609 --> 00:02:17.926
She was still wearing the ring.

33
00:02:17.927 --> 00:02:21.474
Even as she spoke, she started to grow.

34
00:02:21.475 --> 00:02:25.270
Soon she was four meters high.

35
00:02:25.271 --> 00:02:28.275
But she didn't grow much in width.

36
00:02:28.276 --> 00:02:31.469
So she was very, very skinny.

37
00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:37.048
"Oh, Mabel, that was silly," said Kathleen.

38
00:02:37.049 --> 00:02:40.622
"Who knows how long this spell will last?"

39
00:02:40.623 --> 00:02:45.761
"What am I going to do now?" moaned Mabel.

40
00:02:45.762 --> 00:02:51.297
"We must hide you until you're back to your right size," said Gerald.

41
00:02:51.298 --> 00:02:54.426
"How about in an empty room?"

42
00:02:54.427 --> 00:02:58.479
"I'd rather stay outside," said Mabel.

43
00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:02.531
"It's a good thing my aunt thinks I'm staying overnight with you."

44
00:03:02.532 --> 00:03:05.160
The children went outside.

45
00:03:05.161 --> 00:03:09.736
Mabel had to crawl to fit through doors.

46
00:03:09.737 --> 00:03:14.447
Outside she crept behind some bushes so no one would see her.

47
00:03:14.448 --> 00:03:18.022
"Aren't you hungry?" asked Jimmy.

48
00:03:18.023 --> 00:03:21.209
"Oh yes," said Mabel.

49
00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:25.751
"I'll write to my aunt, and she'll send us a picnic."

50
00:03:25.752 --> 00:03:31.026
Mabel used Gerald's notebook to write a note.

51
00:03:31.027 --> 00:03:34.631
Dear Aunt, May we have some things for a picnic?

52
00:03:34.632 --> 00:03:36.046
Gerald will bring them.

53
00:03:36.047 --> 00:03:38.560
I'd come myself, but I'm tired.

54
00:03:38.561 --> 00:03:41.281
I think I've been growing rather fast.

55
00:03:41.282 --> 00:03:44.874
Your loving niece, Mabel

56
00:03:44.875 --> 00:03:51.715
Gerald went to fetch the food.

57
00:03:51.716 --> 00:03:58.302
When he came back, they had a splendid picnic of bread, cake, gooseberries, and milk.

58
00:03:58.303 --> 00:04:02.119
Gerald noticed the dinosaur statue nearby.

59
00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:05.628
"He must have eaten some good meals in his time."

60
00:04:05.629 --> 00:04:10.929
Kathleen giggled. "We fed him today."

61
00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:14.164
"What do you mean?" asked Jimmy.

62
00:04:14.165 --> 00:04:21.501
Kathleen explained how she and Mabel had hidden the Ugly-Wuglies' clothes in the dinosaur's belly.

63
00:04:21.502 --> 00:04:25.873
"We can take them home now," said Gerald.

64
00:04:25.874 --> 00:04:29.739
"I've got an idea," Kathleen suddenly said.

65
00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:36.779
"Give me the ring."

66
00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:40.480
She ran ahead of the others.

67
00:04:40.481 --> 00:04:43.860
"I say this is a wishing ring."

68
00:04:43.861 --> 00:04:48.065
She believed the ring would change if she renamed it.

69
00:04:48.066 --> 00:04:54.192
When they reached the dinosaur, Kathleen climbed up into its belly.

70
00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:59.048
She handed down the clothes and other Ugly-Wugly things to her brothers.

71
00:04:59.049 --> 00:05:04.872
"Wait a minute," said Gerald. "I'm coming up."

72
00:05:04.873 --> 00:05:08.762
"Isn't it nice in here?" said Kathleen.

73
00:05:08.763 --> 00:05:13.162
"I wish I were a statue. Oh!"

74
00:05:13.163 --> 00:05:20.914
And just like that, Kathleen turned into a statue.

